{
  "_doc": "harness-downshift embedded catalog — model data lives here, not in Go source.",
  "_doc2": "Override at ~/.harness-downshift/catalog.json. Run 'downshift models pull' to refresh.",
  "_doc3": "'family' is the stable prefix for version-agnostic matching. A model whose ID starts with the family string matches this entry's tier even if the exact version is unknown.",
  "_doc4": "OpenRouter model IDs arrive as 'provider/model-id' (e.g. 'anthropic/claude-opus-5-5'). The router normalises these before lookup, so family matching works transparently.",
  "_doc5": "Anthropic IDs and base input/output prices per 1M tokens, verified 2026-10-19 against https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing (formerly docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/pricing) and https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview. Cache write (5m) is 1.25x input for every Anthropic model. Cache read is 0.1x input, except Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Sonnet 5.5 (0.05x, so Sonnet 5.5 reads at $0.10 on $2.00 input) and Claude Fable 5.1 (0.025x). An exact-id row exists for each older model that a 5.x row used to alias (claude-sonnet-4-6, claude-opus-4-8, claude-fable-5): they have different list prices and must not share a row.",
  "_doc9": "prices_as_of is the date the list prices were last verified against a public source. The weekly workflow .github/workflows/sync-prices.yml runs scripts/sync_catalog_prices.py (OpenRouter public model list, no key) and opens a PR when a price or the date changes. downshift doctor warns when prices_as_of is more than 30 days old. Savings figures are estimates at these list prices. See docs/reference/prices.md.",
  "_doc8": "Optional cache_read_cost_per_1m / cache_write_cost_per_1m come from the OpenRouter price snapshot dated 2026-10-12 (research/prices/effort-capabilities-2026-10-12.json), written by scripts/sync_catalog_prices.py for entries whose id matches a snapshot model id exactly. Absent means no cache price: cost then bills cached tokens at the input rate, an upper bound. Since 2026-10-19 the weekly sync-prices workflow re-runs the script against the live OpenRouter list (see _doc9), for the claude-code, codex and kirocrew harnesses. Codex input and cached-input prices were checked against https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing on 2026-10-19; OpenAI lists no cache-write price, so a codex cache_write figure is OpenRouter's.",
  "_doc7": "Optional 'efforts': allowed effort values for the model, listed ONLY where verified against vendor docs on 2026-10-12. Absent means unknown: no restriction is applied and nothing is assumed.",
  "_doc6": "Claude Code's native alias 'haiku' resolves to claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (Claude Code 2.1.289, observed 2026-10-15 in eval run b5/mech-rename/claude-routed-force-r1: stream lines, resolved records and Claude Code's own modelUsage), so the claude-code small entry is claude-haiku-4-5 at $1.00/$5.00, cache $0.10 read / $1.25 write per 1M. claude-haiku-5-5 ($0.10/$0.50 up to 100k prompt tokens, $0.50/$2.50 above; the catalog stores the up-to-100k price, so above 100k the gap to the frontier model is ~87%, not ~97%) is its own claude-code entry with no native name and no family: it is priced only on its exact id and is never the automatic small target. Older claude-haiku-4-5 ids match through the claude-haiku family; they are not an alias of 5-5 because KiroCrew owns that canonical id.",
  "version": "2",
  "updated": "2026-10-19",
  "prices_as_of": "2026-10-19",
